{"id": "unknown-2026-11-13-026", "date": "2026-11-13", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 46, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Cetus seals $200m share placement ahead of Oslo debut", "content": "<p>Hong Kong-based dry bulk owner Cetus Maritime has successfully placed a NOK1.89bn ($200m) share offering, including an over-allotment, clearing a major hurdle ahead of its planned Oslo stock market debut next week. The Mark Young-led company said it had conditionally allocated 108.5m shares at NOK17.44 ($1.83) apiece, taking up the full $25m over-allotment on top &#8230;</p>\n</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "splash247", "url": "https://splash247.com/cetus-seals-200m-share-placement-ahead-of-oslo-debut/", "type": "rss"}]}
